{
  // Solution file: `tsc -b` walks these references; it compiles nothing itself.
  // Every workspace tsconfig extends ./tsconfig.base.json and sets composite: true.
  //
  // ORDER IS THE LAYERING LAW (design/W1-STACK-SPEC.md §2), read bottom-up:
  // the {errors, events} kernel imports nothing, platform leaves import only the
  // kernel, verticals sit on platform, @app/api composes verticals, and the two
  // apps sit on top. `tsc -b` derives its own build order from the per-package
  // `references`, so this list is a manifest, not a schedule — but keeping it in
  // layer order means a reference added in the wrong place reads as wrong here.
  //
  // The `contracts` gate cross-checks this list against the pnpm workspace graph:
  // three parallel topologies (workspace deps, project references, the knip map)
  // desynchronise into type errors that point everywhere except at the drift.
  //
  // A vertical's package goes directly above @app/api. The installer DERIVES two kinds
  // of entry rather than shipping them here, because a reference to a project that does
  // not exist kills `tsc -b` on its first line: an enabled module's package, and the
  // demo vertical `init --with-demo` plants (installer/lib/tsconfig-references.mjs).
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "packages/platform/errors" },
    { "path": "packages/platform/events" },
    { "path": "packages/platform/env" },
    { "path": "packages/platform/observability" },
    { "path": "packages/platform/ratelimit" },
    { "path": "packages/platform/supabase" },
    { "path": "packages/contracts" },
    { "path": "packages/design-tokens" },
    { "path": "packages/design-system" },
    { "path": "packages/design-system-native" },
    { "path": "packages/api" }
    // apps/web and apps/mobile are DELIBERATELY absent. They are build LEAVES (nothing
    // imports them), non-composite + noEmit, so a reference here would red with
    // "referenced project must have composite: true". They are typechecked as their own
    // `tsc -b` build roots — see the `types` step in tools/harness.config.mjs, which runs
    // `tsc -b . apps/web apps/mobile`. Their own `references` pull in the composite
    // packages they depend on, so build order is correct. SOURCE: design/W1-STACK-SPEC.md §3
  ]
}
